From 804d982cd2bb3714d4c85b4764ea61e4df1f0711 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunstbanause <3209654+Kunstbanause@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:36:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] c/main: Camera passthrough in the compute layer
 squasher

Draw the device's passthrough camera images (get_passthrough_frames)
as a pseudo layer in layer.comp: every view ray hits a sphere around
the eye (XRT_PASSTHROUGH_DISTANCE_M, default 2 m), that point is moved
into the camera with the head pose at capture time and projected with
the camera's Fisheye62 model. Head motion between capture and display
is compensated, the room stays put while the head moves.

- Behind all layers when the frame uses the alpha blend environment
  mode (WayVR with "Enable passthrough").
- Over the main app's layers but under overlay sessions when the
  device's forced flag is set, faded in and out
  (XRT_PASSTHROUGH_FADE_S). The multi compositor now tells the native
  compositor how many layers at the end come from overlay sessions
  (xrt_layer_frame_data::overlay_layer_count), so WayVR stays usable
  on top of the room.

The images are uploaded through persistently mapped staging buffers
recorded into the frame's command buffer, only when a new image
arrived. The one projection layer fast path is skipped while
passthrough is shown. Nothing is done while it is off. Compute path
only (the desktop default). XRT_PASSTHROUGH_GAIN scales brightness,
XRT_PASSTHROUGH_STATS=1 logs a summary once a second, the debug UI has
"Compositor: Passthrough".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
